timeline.body:
Could you put the body of this method on `IpPrefix` itself? That's how the rest of Elasticsearch works. ESQL works this way for a reason that we're in the process of making not true any more. The general pattern is
```
public IpPrefix(Source, Field, Field) { <-- the "normal" ctro
}

public IpPrefix(PlanStreamInput in) throws IOException { <-- the "streaming" ctor
}

public void writeTo(PlanStreamOutput out) throws IOException {
}
```

The important bit is that the streaming ctor and `writeTo` fit on the same screen. So we stick them next to each other. That way you can read them and use you eyes to check if they are a mirror of one another quickly.

